{"slug": "kale-tabbouleh", "nyt_id": 12915, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12915-kale-tabbouleh", "name": "Kale Tabbouleh", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "Here’s the thing about tabbouleh salad: Most of the ones I’ve had invert my preferred proportion of bulgur to parsley. What you usually get is a bowl of tabbouleh studded with bits of parsley. I like a salad that is mostly parsley, studded with grains of tabbouleh. I pictured a generous ratio of green to tan, but with kale standing in for parsley. It has a hint of parsley’s pleasing bitterness, but is far milder, which means that this tabbouleh salad didn’t have to be just a side dish, one best eaten in small portions. Instead, I could eat a whole bowl of it — a dream for a raw kale devotee.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "⅔ cup fine bulgur", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "fine bulgur", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 tablespoons lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 shallot, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallot", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 teaspoons ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 ¼ teaspoons fine sea salt, more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": "more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup extra-virgin olive oil, more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": "more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 bunch kale, stems removed, leaves finely chopped (5 cups)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "bunch", "item": "kale", "preparation": "stems removed, leaves finely chopped (5 cups)", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 large ripe tomatoes, diced (about 2 cups)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large ripe tomatoes", "preparation": "diced (about 2 cups)", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup torn mint leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "torn mint leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup diced radish", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "diced radish", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Black pepper, as needed", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "black pepper", "preparation": "as needed", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Cook bulgur according to package instructions. Cool."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a small bowl, whisk together lemon juice, shallot, cumin and salt. Whisk in olive oil."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a large bowl, toss together bulgur, kale, tomatoes, mint and radish. Toss in dressing. Season with black pepper and more salt if you like, and drizzle with additional oil if desired."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 247.0, "protein_g": 3.7, "carbohydrates_g": 18.7, "fat_g": 18.9, "saturated_fat_g": 2.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 346.9, "fiber_g": 4.6, "sugar_g": 3.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 15.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mediterranean"],